<title>UK: Boots climbs as Merrill says &quot;accumulate&quot;.</title>
<headline>Boots climbs as Merrill says &quot;accumulate&quot;.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in pharmacy and retailing group Boots Co Plc climbed on Wednesday after analysts at Merrill Lynch met with the company and retained a positive stance on the stock.</p>
<p>The shares were up 10p to 706-1/2p by 1401 GMT.</p>
<p>Market sources said the analysts had recently met with the company and still preferred the stock to retailer W.H. Smith, but the analysts were unavailable for immediate comment.</p>
<p>--Elaine Hardcastle, London Newsroom +44 171 542 4027</p>
